  "engine": "FFmpeg xfade",
  "verifiedAgainst": "FFmpeg 7.1.5 xfade help in independent test environment",
  "filterDocs": "https://ffmpeg.org/ffmpeg-filters.html#xfade",
  "licenseUrl": "https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html",
  "intendedUse": "Optional offline transition design for original source footage, independent of any particular editing app",
  "limitations": [
    "Check the installed FFmpeg xfade filter with `ffmpeg -hide_banner -h filter=xfade`; not every build/version supports the same options.",
    "Both video inputs must share constant frame rate, resolution, pixel format, frame rate and time base. Normalize before xfade. Validate sample aspect ratio.",
    "Set offset relative to the first clip's timeline (often first clip duration minus overlap duration). Make overlap shorter than each clip.",
    "xfade handles video only. Process audio separately when needed (for instance, acrossfade), respecting source music licenses and sound balance.",
    "Many effects should be used sparingly and chosen to fit motion, narrative and accessibility. Flash effects can be uncomfortable for sensitive viewers.",
    "Using a free executable does not license the input video, music or sound files. FFmpeg distribution obligations depend on how FFmpeg was built."
  ],
